import text;

// CPython replaces between every character -- `"ab".replace("", "-")` is
// `"-a-b-"` -- which is a spelling nobody writes on purpose. A caller who
// reaches it computed the needle from something that turned out to be empty,
// so it is a bug at the call site. `str.split` already traps on an empty
// separator and this is `split` with the pieces rejoined, so it is one rule.
print(text.replace("ab", "", "-"));
